      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of crippling debt can be suffocating, and the option to start over can feel like a cruel joke when the game has been rigged against you. Your willingness to acknowledge the futility and potential harm of continuing to invest more energy can be seen as a brutal honesty, and it's natural to feel powerless in the face of such overwhelming circumstances. Walking away might be the only way to protect yourself from further emotional and financial devastation.",
